  "solution": {
    "text": "The direction of the velocity of the particle may be shown as in the diagram. This velocity V<sub>0</sub> is resolved in two components. Here <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>V</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>cos</mo><mi>&#945;</mi></math> component is tangential horizontal and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>V</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>sin</mo><mi>&#945;</mi></math> is along the surface but vertically downwards. Here, if the particle exerts a force N on the surface of the cylinder, the cylinder will also apply equal and opposite force on the particle<br /><br /><br />&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; <u><strong><img alt=\"\" src=\"https://cdn-question-pool.getmarks.app/nta_abhyas/jee_main/images/EM0027045_ANs_.jpg\" style=\"max-width:100%; object-fit:contain\" style=\"width: 160px; height: 200px;\" /></strong></u><br /><br /><br />and this will provide a centripetal force to the particle.<br /><br />So,&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mtext mathvariant=\"italic\">N</mtext><mo>=</mo><mtext mathvariant=\"italic\">m</mtext><msup><mfenced><mrow><msub><mtext mathvariant=\"italic\">V</mtext><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>cos</mo><mi>&#945;</mi></mrow></mfenced><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>/</mo><mtext mathvariant=\"italic\">R</mtext></math><br /><br />&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>=</mo><msubsup><mtext mathvariant=\"italic\">mV</mtext><mn>0</mn><mn>2</mn></msubsup><msup><mtext>cos</mtext><mn>2</mn></msup><mi>&#945;</mi><mo>/</mo><mtext mathvariant=\"italic\">R</mtext></math><br /><br />or, &nbsp;&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mtext mathvariant=\"italic\">N</mtext><mo>=</mo><mfrac><msubsup><mtext mathvariant=\"italic\">mV</mtext><mn>0</mn><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mtext mathvariant=\"italic\">R</mtext></mfrac><msup><mtext>cos</mtext><mn>2</mn></msup><mi>&#945;</mi></math>",
